Est       - 1.85 kcal/mol added to the activation energy of 1-octyl 1,6 H-shift (primary <=> secondary) kinf and k0 rate constants. 
              This value comes from the difference of the slopes (lnk=f(1/T)) of rate constants for 1,5 H-shift 
              for 1-octyl = 4-octyl (primary <=> secondary) and 2-octyl = 3-octyl (secondary<=>secondary) from 08TSAb 

Est-2     - 1-hexyl = 2-hexyl rate constant (kinf) from 07TSA fitted to a 2 parameters Arrhenius. 
            1-hexen-6-yl = 1-hexen-3-yl rate constant (kinf) from 09TSA fitted to a 2 parameters Arrhenius. The difference of the slope between this two set of rate is 4.9 kcal/mol.
            Rate constant finally used: 1-heptyl = 3-heptyl high pressure limit rate constant fitted to a 2 parameter Arrhenius and Ea lowered by 4.9 kcal/mol. 
